From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:05:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: include the Lineage libion sepolicy

system/sepolicy 9b2d37dc2 (Android 17) dropped the /dev/ion file_contexts
entry and every coredomain ion_device rule, so the node is labeled
`device` and nothing in the tree relabels it. On this kernel gralloc,
Adreno, QSEECom and keymaster all allocate through /dev/ion: enforcing,
qseecomd (tee) and keymaster-3-0 are denied the open at 13 s and the
composer cannot allocate. device/lineage/sepolicy/libion carries the
removed rules; include it the way bonito does.

---
 BoardConfigCommon.mk | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/BoardConfigCommon.mk b/BoardConfigCommon.mk
index 78d0d83a..7390d800 100644
--- a/BoardConfigCommon.mk
+++ b/BoardConfigCommon.mk
@@ -161,6 +161,8 @@ include device/qcom/sepolicy-legacy-um/SEPolicy.mk
 include hardware/sony/timekeep/sepolicy/SEPolicy.mk
 BOARD_VENDOR_SEPOLICY_DIRS += $(COMMON_PATH)/sepolicy/vendor
 PRODUCT_PRIVATE_SEPOLICY_DIRS += $(COMMON_PATH)/sepolicy/private
+# ION labeling and coredomain rules left system/sepolicy in Android 17 (9b2d37dc2); this kernel has no dmabuf heaps
+include device/lineage/sepolicy/libion/sepolicy.mk
 SELINUX_IGNORE_NEVERALLOWS := true
 
 # Verity
